crates/mdbook-compare/README.md
     1→# mdbook-compare

crates/mdbook-core/README.md
     1→# mdbook-core
     7→This is the base support library for [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/). It is intended for internal use only. Other mdBook crates depend on this for any types that are shared across the crates.
     8→
     9→> This crate is maintained by the mdBook team, primarily for use by mdBook and not intended for external use (except as a transitive dependency). This crate may make major changes to its APIs or be deprecated without warning.
    10→

crates/mdbook-driver/README.md
     1→# mdbook-driver
     7→This is the high-level Rust library for running [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/). New books can be created using [`BookBuilder`](https://docs.rs/mdbook-driver/latest/mdbook_driver/init/struct.BookBuilder.html). The primary type [`MDBook`](https://docs.rs/mdbook-driver/latest/mdbook_driver/struct.MDBook.html) can be used to manage and render books.
     8→
     9→> This crate is maintained by the mdBook team for use by the wider ecosystem. This crate follows [semver compatibility](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/semver.html) for its APIs.
    10→

crates/mdbook-html/README.md
     1→# mdbook-html
     7→This is the HTML renderer for [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/). This is intended for internal use only. It is automatically included by [`mdbook-driver`](https://crates.io/crates/mdbook-driver) to render books to HTML.
     8→
     9→> This crate is maintained by the mdBook team, primarily for use by mdBook and not intended for external use (except as a transitive dependency). This crate may make major changes to its APIs or be deprecated without warning.
    10→

crates/mdbook-markdown/README.md
     1→# mdbook-markdown
     7→This is the Markdown support library for [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/). Rust crates (such as preprocessors) can use this library to process Markdown in the same way as mdBook.
     8→
     9→> This crate is maintained by the mdBook team for use by the wider ecosystem. This crate follows [semver compatibility](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/semver.html) for its APIs.
    10→

crates/mdbook-preprocessor/README.md
     1→# mdbook-preprocessor
     7→This is the Rust library to implement a [preprocessor](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/for_developers/preprocessors.html) for [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/).
     8→
     9→> This crate is maintained by the mdBook team for use by the wider ecosystem. This crate follows [semver compatibility](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/semver.html) for its APIs.
    10→

crates/mdbook-renderer/README.md
     1→# mdbook-renderer
     7→This is the Rust library to implement a [renderer](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/for_developers/backends.html) for [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/).
     8→
     9→> This crate is maintained by the mdBook team for use by the wider ecosystem. This crate follows [semver compatibility](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/semver.html) for its APIs.
    10→

crates/mdbook-summary/README.md
     1→# mdbook-summary
     7→This is the Rust library used to parse the [`SUMMARY.md`](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/format/summary.html) file structure for [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/).
     8→
     9→> This crate is maintained by the mdBook team for use by the wider ecosystem. This crate follows [semver compatibility](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/semver.html) for its APIs.
    10→

crates/xtask/README.md
     1→# xtask
     3→This is a CLI utility for running development commands for mdbook.
     4→See [CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md) for how to use this.

